<!-- ================= FEATURES ================= -->
<section class="features" id="cars">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Crew manifest · what's aboard</p>
        <h2 data-reveal data-d="80">Three reasons the desert<br>is better lying down.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="aside" data-reveal data-d="160">Eleven carriages,<br>one kitchen car,<br>zero hurry.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="manifest">
      <article class="row-feature" data-reveal>
        <div class="idx">01</div>
        <div class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M4 23h24"/><path d="M8 23a8 8 0 0 1 16 0"/><path d="M16 11v-4"/><circle cx="16" cy="5" r="1.4"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>The Glass Lookout<small>Car 3 · swivel seating · dimmed at 22:00</small></h3>
        <p>Half this carriage is a window. Its arched glass runs clean over the ceiling, so when the sun drops behind the western ridges the whole desert turns rose-glass for about nineteen minutes. Sand foxes are reported most nights around <b>kilometre 640</b>. Lantern policy: candle-temperature light only.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="row-feature" data-reveal>
        <div class="idx">02</div>
        <div class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M4 23h24"/><path d="M8 23a8 8 0 0 1 16 0"/><circle cx="16" cy="13" r="1.6"/><path d="M12 6q2 2 0 4M20 6q2 2 0 4"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>The Caravan Kitchen<small>Single seating · 22:00 sharp · lamp-lit</small></h3>
        <p>A four-course desert menu cooked from what actually grows along the line — saltbush, tepary beans, dates off the oasis oasts. The chef presents every course with the <b>kilometre it was dreamed up at</b>, so dinner becomes a kind of slow地图 of the route. Coffee is served exactly as the moon clears the plateau.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="row-feature" data-reveal>
        <div class="idx">03</div>
        <div class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 25h24"/><path d="M6 25v-9M26 25v-9"/><path d="M6 17h20"/><path d="M16 9l1.2 2.4 2.4.4-1.8 1.7.5 2.5-2.3-1.3-2.3 1.3.5-2.5-1.8-1.7 2.4-.4z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Starlight Berths<small>Cars 6–8 · ceilings fold open to the sky</small></h3>
        <p>Every cabin ceiling folds back to bare sky; there is no glass between the mattress and the Milky Way, only waxed canvas if you insist. Wool mattresses, cedar-lined drawers, and a porter who wakes you <b>twenty minutes before Neon Harbor — never earlier</b>.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

